### Step 2: Analyzing the Condition \( f(s) - s \not\equiv 0 \mod 3 \)

We need to determine which elements in \( S \) can be part of cycles under the modulo 3 condition. The set \( S \) can be partitioned into three residue classes modulo 3:
- Elements congruent to 0 modulo 3: \{3, 6, 9\}
- Elements congruent to 1 modulo 3: \{1, 4, 7\}
